        <item>
            <title>1.3.24</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:31:46 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>10324</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.3.24</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MotionUI 1.3.24</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Three new easing curves next to expo. Swing In and Swing Out are a pair: the speed at the end of one matches the speed at the start of the other, so a movement carries across a hard cut without a jump. Wave runs fast, slow, fast in a single move.</li>
  <li>Swing Through, in the Easing section. Pick it like a curve, set Flow, and a whole chain of keyframes runs as one move: the keys in between slow down but never stop, and the first and the last key end up at the same speed.</li>
  <li>Claude can now change the fill color and the stroke of a shape that already exists. A shape drawn without a stroke gets one, placed above the fill.</li>
  <li>Claude can move a layer to any position in the stack, so new layers no longer have to stay on top.</li>
  <li>Tracking can be animated. It rides on its own text animator, which a text effect no longer takes with it.</li>
  <li>Layers whose name is a number, like "100", can be addressed by that name again instead of being read as a layer index.</li>
  <li>Windows: the installers are signed.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
